    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203651701?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fix two spelling mistakes reported by the weekly spelling check and add repository-specific/example tokens to the project dictionary so the spell-checker no longer flags them.</p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">files/en-us/web/api/gputexture/createview/index.md — grba → rgba</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">files/en-us/web/css/reference/properties/text-decoration-inset/index.md — appearence → appearance</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add .vscode/dictionaries/en-custom.txt containing repository/example tokens so they are ignored by the spell-checker.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The automated Weekly Spelling Check reported two genuine typos and several valid technical/example tokens that are not present in the repository dictionary. F</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These values are example identifiers, person names, URL schemes, and OTP token strings used in MDN examples.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42068.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3656625072\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42068\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42068/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42068\">#42068</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42080",
            "title": "Fix typos and add dictionary entries (fixes #42068)",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T11:53:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T11:48:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BurramsettyAkshayaPranathi",
                "url": "https://github.com/BurramsettyAkshayaPranathi"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32789589?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updated the order for the rotationRate property fields the match the definition in the standard.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The current order does not follow what is defined in the W3S standard of the <code class=\"notranslate\">DeviceMotionEvent</code> properties or the current documentation of the <code class=\"notranslate\">acceleration</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">accelerationIncludingGravity</code> property.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Matches what is defined in the W3S standard: <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/deviceorientation/#device-motion-event-rotation-rate-api\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/deviceorientation/#device-motion-event-rotation-rate-api</a><br>\nAligns with the documentation of the acceleration property: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DeviceMotionEvent/acceleration\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DeviceMotionEvent/acceleration</a><br>\nand accelerationIncludingGravity property: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DeviceMotionEvent/accelerationIncludingGravity\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DeviceMotionEvent/accelerationIncludingGravity</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">None that I can find</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42079",
            "title": "Fix rotationRate property descriptions order",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T11:21:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T11:21:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "antonegas",
                "url": "https://github.com/antonegas"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/576623?u=88392c52422628facfd7cf108241d2864680915d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1744292\" rel=\"nofollow\">Firefox 146 added</a> support for <code class=\"notranslate\">@custom-media</code> at-rule, enabling developers to use custom media variables inside <code class=\"notranslate\">@media</code> at-rules.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28438\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28438/hovercard\">I already updated BCD</a>, and created a <a href=\"https://web-platform-dx.github.io/web-features-explorer/features/custom-media-queries/\" rel=\"nofollow\">web feature</a> on web platform. This PR adds an article to MDN explaining how and when to use <strong>Custom Media Queries</strong>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Over a year ago <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/35755\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/35755/hovercard\">I tried to add this article</a> but <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/35755#issuecomment-2423263341\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/35755/hovercard\">it was denied</a> as no browser implemented this feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Now, with Firefox implementing it, we can add an article, explaining how to use this feature.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42075",
            "title": "Add CSS `@custom-media` at-rule",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T08:36:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T07:52:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ramiy",
                "url": "https://github.com/ramiy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The worker constructor takes a <code class=\"notranslate\">url</code> parameter that that can be a <code class=\"notranslate\">TrustedScriptURL</code>. This attempts to follow the pattern of our other trusted types docs and add the header warning and security considerations section.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note this is draft because I am trying to tidy up other inconsistencies with the documentation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related project: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510273732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\">#41507</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42073",
            "title": "Worker() constructor - update for TT",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T06:39:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T06:28:07.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates <code class=\"notranslate\">Window.setTimeout()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">WorkerGlobalScope.setTimeout()</code> for trusted types, following the same approach as <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3650316385\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42042\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42042/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42042\">#42042</a></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>More or less full docs in the windows method. There is a page header warning in the top and a security considerations section in the body.</li>\n<li>worker method has same top section, but description and examples are cross linked to window method docs. The header links to the security considerations in the window method topic.</li>\n<li>Examples do not cover the use of TT. We have pretty strong warnings up the top about using this feature at all, so I don't see we need to show TT use.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This also did some consistency fixes across both this and the <code class=\"notranslate\">setInterval</code> methods so that they have the same name for the function param (<code class=\"notranslate\">func</code>) and the arguments are referred to as <code class=\"notranslate\">param</code> rather than <code class=\"notranslate\">args</code> - which is consistent with the template for web apis.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There were a few layout change and improvements to the docs - these map the similar changes done previously for <code class=\"notranslate\">setInterval()</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is part of project being tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510273732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\">#41507</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42072",
            "title": "setTimeout() on Window/Worker plus consistency fixes",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T06:05:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T04:58:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF146 adds support for the MathML CSS <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/math-shift\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">math-shift</code></a> property.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds adds a release note and also fixes up the example which wasn't working properly.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3607745179\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41877\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41877/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41877\">#41877</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42069",
            "title": "Ff146 css math shift",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T00:07:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T00:04:43.000Z",
